 ## Overview
-This method computes the Signed Distance Function (SDF) value for each voxel in a grid by evaluating an implicit surface primitive. It serves as the core evaluation step within batched SDF inference pipelines, transforming grid indices to world space and applying the shape's geometric function. It differs from higher-level ray marching by operating on a discrete voxel grid rather than continuous rays, and from mesh generation by outputting scalar field values rather than topology.
+SDF Value Computation is the core kernel that calculates the Signed Distance Function (SDF) value for each voxel in a grid. It transforms grid coordinates to world space, evaluates the SDF function, and stores the result. It builds on [Batched SDF Inference](2329-batched-sdf-inference.md) by performing the actual geometric evaluation for a batch of samples.
 
